  "reasoning": "The complete bipartite graph K_{8,8} on 16 vertices (partition vertices 0-7 and 8-15) is triangle-free because any triangle would require two vertices from the same partition to be adjacent, but edges only exist between partitions. It is maximal because adding any edge within a partition would create a triangle: any two vertices in the same partition share all 8 vertices in the opposite partition as common neighbors, so adding an edge between them immediately forms a triangle. This achieves the maximum possible 64 edges for a triangle-free graph on 16 vertices (Mantel's theorem).",
